<%- include('partials/header') %>

<div class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">History</p>
    <h1>Import past expenses</h1>
    <p class="sub">
        Bring in spending from before you started using Ledger. These are
        saved as historical records only — no account balance changes.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="grid-2">

    <div class="card">
        <h2>Paste your data</h2>

        <form method="POST" action="/import-expenses" class="form">
            <input
                type="hidden"
                name="csrf_token"
                value="<%= csrfToken %>"
            >

            <label>
                One entry per line
                <span class="optional">date, amount, note (note is optional)</span>
                <textarea
                    name="data"
                    rows="12"
                    required
                    placeholder="2026-01-01, 250
2026-01-02, 180, Auto fare
05-01-2026, 620
06/01/2026 340 Groceries"
                ></textarea>
            </label>

            <button class="btn btn-primary btn-block">
                Import records
            </button>
        </form>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2>Format</h2>

        <ul class="hint-list">
            <li>One day's spending per line.</li>
            <li>Separate the date and amount with a comma or a space.</li>
            <li>Dates can be <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code> or <code>DD-MM-YYYY</code> (also with <code>/</code>).</li>
            <li>An optional third value is saved as a note.</li>
            <li>Blank lines are ignored.</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="hint">
            Imported entries are tagged
            <strong>“Imported (Historical)”</strong>
            and show up in your Expenses list, Reports, and monthly trend —
            but they never touch a Cash, Online, or any other account
            balance, since the money was already spent before Ledger
            existed for you.
        </p>

        <p class="hint">
            If anything in your paste can't be read, nothing is imported —
            you'll get a list of the exact lines to fix, then you can
            paste again.
        </p>
    </div>

</div>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
